WEBVTT

00:35:28.400 --> 00:35:31.296
Tracy Dumas and Jill Perry-Smith
on absorption at work,

00:35:31.320 --> 00:35:34.476
and Bob Boice on scheduling
writing sessions.

00:35:34.500 --> 00:35:35.834
And thanks to Candice Faktor

00:35:35.858 --> 00:35:38.886
for the amazing introduction
to Margaret Atwood.

00:35:38.910 --> 00:35:42.449
(Music)

00:35:43.611 --> 00:35:45.666
MA: OK, so here's the story.

00:35:45.690 --> 00:35:48.326
We were throwing a party
at our house for some writers.

00:35:48.350 --> 00:35:50.255
And there they were, all milling around.

00:35:50.279 --> 00:35:54.016
And then this young woman,
who was about 35,

00:35:54.040 --> 00:35:56.396
said she was having a heart attack.

00:35:56.420 --> 00:35:59.914
Then I called 911
and the paramedics arrived,

00:35:59.938 --> 00:36:02.166
lumpety-bump up the steps.